; The installer's and uninstaller's own words in English, which tauri.conf.json names in
; customLanguageFiles in place of Tauri's (18 October 2026, the fourth Tauri build). Every name Tauri
; uses here is kept, since its installer script asks for each. Since the fifth build (18 October, Adam's
; word after the fourth build's screenshots) every line is said plainly: no exclamation marks, nothing
; "recommended", no "operation", short sentences saying what happens. The page that holds the long
; lines gives them three lines at most. The uninstaller's tick says what it clears, where Tauri's
; "Delete the application data" read as deleting his cases, and the lines about an open Idiograph never
; speak of killing it. Six lines are the screenshot check's words since the sixth build (18 October, Adam's
; yes): the page an older Setup shows where a newer version is installed, its second choice, the same
; Setup run silently, and the three about Microsoft's WebView2.
LangString addOrReinstall ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Install it again"
LangString alreadyInstalled ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Already installed"
LangString alreadyInstalledLong ${LANG_ENGLISH} "${PRODUCTNAME} ${VERSION} is already installed. Choose what to do, then click Next."
LangString appRunning ${LANG_ENGLISH} "${PRODUCTNAME} is open. Quit it, then try again."
LangString appRunningOkKill ${LANG_ENGLISH} "${PRODUCTNAME} is open.$\nPress OK to close it."
LangString chooseMaintenanceOption ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Install it again, or uninstall it."
LangString choowHowToInstall ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Choose how to install ${PRODUCTNAME}."
LangString createDesktop ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Create desktop shortcut"
LangString dontUninstall ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Install over it"
LangString dontUninstallDowngrade ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Install over it (not possible with an older version)"
LangString failedToKillApp ${LANG_ENGLISH} "${PRODUCTNAME} could not be closed. Quit it, then try again."
LangString installingWebview2 ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Installing Microsoft's WebView2, which ${PRODUCTNAME} needs"
LangString newerVersionInstalled ${LANG_ENGLISH} "A newer version of ${PRODUCTNAME} is installed. This Setup is older. Choose what to do, then click Next."
LangString older ${LANG_ENGLISH} "older"
LangString olderOrUnknownVersionInstalled ${LANG_ENGLISH} "An $R4 version of ${PRODUCTNAME} is installed. Choose what to do, then click Next."
LangString silentDowngrades ${LANG_ENGLISH} "A newer version of ${PRODUCTNAME} is installed, so this older one was not installed. Double-click this installer to choose what to do.$\n"
LangString unableToUninstall ${LANG_ENGLISH} "The installed ${PRODUCTNAME} could not be uninstalled."
LangString uninstallApp ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Uninstall ${PRODUCTNAME}"
LangString uninstallBeforeInstalling ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Uninstall it first"
LangString unknown ${LANG_ENGLISH} "unknown"
LangString webview2AbortError ${LANG_ENGLISH} "WebView2 did not install, and ${PRODUCTNAME} needs it. Run this installer again."
LangString webview2DownloadError ${LANG_ENGLISH} "WebView2 did not download ($0). Check you are online, then run this installer again."
LangString webview2DownloadSuccess ${LANG_ENGLISH} "WebView2's installer downloaded"
LangString webview2Downloading ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Downloading WebView2's installer"
LangString webview2InstallError ${LANG_ENGLISH} "WebView2 did not install (code $1). Run this installer again."
LangString webview2InstallSuccess ${LANG_ENGLISH} "WebView2 installed"
LangString deleteAppData ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Also clear the window's size, zoom, appearance and folded sections"
